Local patch, not from upstream. Written against FrankenPHP main at commit f6bb84b
(github.com/php/frankenphp).

php-src commit 37d0ef5a6 (2026-09-29, #23927) removed Zend/zend_atomic.h and the
zend_atomic_* API in favour of C11 atomics: EG(vm_interrupt) and EG(timed_out) are now
atomic_bool. FrankenPHP still uses zend_atomic_bool (two struct fields in frankenphp.h,
plus one static and three zend_atomic_bool_store/load calls in frankenphp.c), so it stops
compiling against php-src master. Upstream had not adapted as of that commit. The typedef
and macros cover frankenphp.c's uses, so the patch only touches the header, and the
__has_include switch keeps builds against php-src without that commit (8.5) on the
original Zend/zend_atomic.h.

The apply step in php/franken{,-testing}/Dockerfile skips this patch once upstream drops
zend_atomic for C11 atomics, so the build picks the fix up on its own. Delete this file
and that block once the skip branch is what fires.

--- a/frankenphp.h
+++ b/frankenphp.h
@@ -20,6 +20,16 @@
 #include <stdbool.h>
 #include <stdint.h>

+#if __has_include(<Zend/zend_atomic.h>)
+#include <Zend/zend_atomic.h>
+#else
+/* php-src 37d0ef5a6 dropped zend_atomic.h; EG(vm_interrupt)/EG(timed_out) are C11 atomic_bool. */
+#include <stdatomic.h>
+typedef atomic_bool zend_atomic_bool;
+#define zend_atomic_bool_store(obj, desired) atomic_store(obj, desired)
+#define zend_atomic_bool_load(obj) atomic_load(obj)
+#endif
+
 #ifndef PHP_WIN32
 #include <pthread.h>
 #include <signal.h>
